description:
Decomposed out of eshyra-o9bd.19.1.1 (PR #475) 2026-07-27, user-approved, after the churn stop rule triggered a SECOND time at efde702.

ROOT ANALYSIS: the registry keeps failing review because it is asked to be AUTHORITATIVE while nothing underwrites its authority. A real source census is deferred (eshyra-s38f, eshyra-o9bd.19.6.1), so every round reviewers correctly find the authority forgeable — mutable contract tables, an evidence taxonomy with no valid home for known-missing clauses, partially captured multi-part evidence, colliding identities. These are symptoms of an authority layer with no source of authority, not independent bugs.

SCOPE — the authority artifacts, to be built against a census that actually exists:
  * canonical facet requirements and implications immutable after import (deep-copy/deep-freeze or immutable accessors), with mutation-attempt regression tests;
  * an evidence taxonomy in which known-missing-source-clause evidence can exist in a valid registry — today it cannot, which is a representational contradiction;
  * multi-part authoritative evidence captured completely, never partially;
  * identity uniqueness across synthetic scalar IDs and ordinary projected atom IDs, which can currently collide.

SEQUENCING: blocked on the source census. Building this before the census repeats the failure.

PR #475 retains the clause completeness CONTRACT — types, facet vocabulary and implications, canonical base requirements, per-clause evaluation, dimension separation — which has stabilised across rounds and is reviewable on its own.
